  "sourceFile": "\"Diocesan Cycle of Prayer, Advent 2026 through Pentecost Season 2026\" -- an 11-page PDF supplied directly by Josh, since the diocese’s own hosted page/PDF (diomass.org) sit behind a client-side bot-protection challenge this session’s sandbox could not pass.",
  "ingested": "2026-09-29",
  "notes": [
    "This diocese is centered on Boston/Eastern Massachusetts, distinct from the already-ingested Diocese of Western Massachusetts (episcopal-western-massachusetts-2026.json) -- not the same file, not a duplicate.",
    "The source document's own title spans Advent 2025 through Pentecost Season 2026 (52 weeks, Nov 30 2025 - Nov 22 2026), arranged alphabetically by deanery. Per this corpus's established precedent for the same shape (see episcopal-atlanta-2026.json and this batch's own episcopal-north-carolina-2026.json), the 5 weeks that fall in calendar year 2025 (Nov 30, Dec 7, 14, 21, 28) are disclosed here but EXCLUDED from `entries`, since they belong to a 2025-dated file this corpus does not maintain (the lopsided 5-vs-47 split matches Atlanta/North Carolina's own precedent for disclose-and-exclude, not Delaware's even-split two-file approach). Those 5 excluded weeks' own subjects (for provenance): Nov 30 -- Church of Our Saviour/St. John's Church/Order of St. Anne & Bethany House of Prayer (all Arlington), The Standing Committee, Brotherhood of St. Gregory; Dec 7 -- St. Paul's Church (Bedford), All Saints' Church (Belmont), St. Mark's Church (Burlington), The Officers of the Diocese, Racial Justice Commission; Dec 14 -- Christ Church/St. Bartholomew's Church/St. James' Church/St. Peter's Church (all Cambridge), Diocesan Disciplinary Board; Dec 21 -- Episcopal Chaplaincy at Harvard, Lutheran Episcopal Chaplaincy at MIT (both Cambridge), The Society of St. John the Evangelist (Cambridge), Hospital Chaplaincies & Healthcare Chaplains; Dec 28 -- Church of Our Redeemer (Lexington), St. James' Church (Somerville), Christ Church (Waltham), Congregation of St. Peter at Christ Episcopal Church (Waltham), Church of the Good Shepherd (Watertown).",
    "A genuine source anomaly: the printed week for 'The Sixth Sunday of Easter' is dated May 19, 2026 and 'The Seventh Sunday of Easter' is dated May 17, 2026 -- printed in that (out-of-chronological) order, and with the Sunday-after-Easter numbering not matching the real 2026 liturgical calendar for either date (Easter 2026 is April 5; the real 6th/7th Sundays of Easter are May 17/24). Both dates' own congregation lists and printed liturgical labels are transcribed exactly as given; only the entry ORDER was corrected (by date) to satisfy this schema's own chronological-order validation rule -- the labels themselves were not corrected, since `liturgicalNote` is a disclosed source label this app never computes or overrides.",
    "Several deanery lists end in a non-parish, no-place entry naming a role or ministry across ALL congregations at once (e.g. 'Congregations: Wardens, Treasurers & Clerks', 'Congregations: Acolytes') -- recorded as `category`, distinct from a single-parish subject.",
    "'Episcopal City Mission' (June 28) is recorded as `category` here since no place is given on this entry -- contrast with the already-ingested Western Massachusetts file, which records the same-named ministry as `parish` on an entry where a place IS given; this is not an inconsistency in this corpus, both entries follow the same place-presence rule.",
    "Entries with 'Chapel' explicitly in the name (St. Andrew's Chapel, Trinity Chapel, St. Aidan's Chapel, Emmanuel Chapel, Grace Chapel, St. John's Chapel/Groton School, St. Mark's Chapel/St. Mark's School, Frank D. Ashburn Chapel/Brooks School) are recorded as `parish`, per this corpus's existing precedent (Delaware's St. Andrew's School Chapel) that a chapel is a worship space even when attached to a school; a school/academy with NO 'Chapel' in its own name (Epiphany School, Esperanza Academy) is recorded as `category` instead, per the same corpus's contrasting precedent (Delaware's St. Anne's School).",
    "Campus ministries and chaplaincies (Northeastern University Lutheran Episcopal Campus Ministry, Boston University Chaplain, Boston College Campus Ministry, Episcopal Chaplaincy at UMass Dartmouth) are recorded as `category`, matching this corpus's existing Chicago/Indianapolis precedent for the same kind of entity.",
    "Religious communities printed in the identical 'Name, Place' comma format as every surrounding parish entry (Allston Abbey, Society of St. Margaret) are recorded as `parish` rather than `category`, matching the format they were actually printed in rather than their institutional character -- disclosed per-subject via `note`.",
    "September 13's 'Trinity Church, Stoughton,' carries a stray trailing comma in the source (an evident print artifact, not additional content) -- transcribed with `place` \"Stoughton\", the stray comma trimmed as punctuation rather than treated as a preserved content typo.",
    "October 4's 'St. Peter' Church/Iglesia de San Pedro, Salem' preserves the source's own missing possessive 's' (\"Peter'\" not \"Peter's\") verbatim.",
    "No entry in this transcribed portion carries a Sunday-after-Pentecost/Proper label separate from its own liturgical name -- both are folded into a single `liturgicalNote` string exactly as printed (e.g. 'The Second Sunday after Pentecost (Proper 5)')."
  ],
